/* book exam traps: DSB-SC is not AM with a small carrier. The carrier is zero, the envelope is |Ac m(t)| and an envelope detector distorts. | A 90° phase error gives zero output, not half. Half output needs 60°, since cos 60° = 0.5. | A frequency error is not a fixed loss: the output is m(t) multiplied by cos 2πΔft, a beat. | Do not draw a line at fc. A tone gives only fc − fm and fc + fm; the bandwidth is still 2W. | The squaring loop output is at 2fc, so it must be divided by 2, and the recovered phase can be 180° off. */
